# Invalidity problems (notation 1).
# Format: see data/README.md. Fields:
#   problem:                 problem name, as shown in the problem list
#   options:                 per-problem options, e.g. eg (a worked example)
#   note:                    note shown under the problem title
#   common-name:             common name of the problem (course database)
#   original-name:           name the problem was copied from
#   errors:                  error count (saved work)
#   seconds:                 time worked, in seconds (saved work)
#   argument:                the argument to show invalid
#   universe-size:           size of the universe
#   interpretation:          interpretations, separated by '.'
#   workspace:               free-form workspace text (encoded)

# baseinvprobs.txt: base homework problems

## 
##                          CHAPTER III
##           MONADIC PREDICATE LOGIC
## 

problem: Inval 3.113
argument: .:  forall x (Fx->forall x Fx)

problem: Inval 3.114
argument: forall x Fx->P  .:  forall x (Fx->P)

problem: Inval 3.115
argument: exists x (Fx->P)  .:  exists x Fx->P

problem: Inval 3.116
argument: .:~(exists x ~Fx&(FA&FB))

problem: Inval 3.117
argument: forall x exists y (Fx<->Gy)  .:  exists y forall x (Fx<->Gy)

problem: Inval 3.118(i)
argument: exists x (Fx&~Gx).  exists x (Gx&~Fx)  .:  forall x (Fx|Gx)

problem: Inval 3.118(iii)
argument: exists x Fx.  exists x Gx.  exists x Hx.  forall x ((Fx&Gx)|(Fx&Hx)|(Gx&Hx)->Jx)  .:  exists x Jx

problem: Inval 3.201
argument: forall x Fx->forall x Gx  .:  forall x (Fx->Gx)

problem: Inval 3.202
argument: .:  exists x (forall y Fy<->~Fx)

problem: Inval 3.203
argument: forall x (Fx<->Gx)  .:  (~exists x Fx&~exists x Gx)|(forall x Fx&forall x Gx)

problem: Inval 3.204
argument: exists x Fx.  forall x Gx  .:  ~forall x (Fx<->Gx)

problem: Inval 3.205
argument: forall x (Fx<->Gx)  .:  (exists x ~Fx->exists x Gx)

problem: Inval 3.206
argument: ~forall x (Fx->Gx)  .:  ~exists x forall y (Fy->Gx)

problem: Inval 3.207
argument: exists x (Fx&Gx)  .:  forall x exists y (Fy&Gx)

